PE 846: Magic Bracelets / 魔法手环

=== Problem Description ===
Bracelet: at least 3 beads in a circle.
Bead numbers: 1, 2, or p^k or 2p^k (odd prime p).
Magic conditions:
  1. All bead numbers distinct
  2. Product of adjacent beads = x^2 + 1
Potency = sum of bead numbers.

=== Allowed numbers ≤ 30 ===
  1  2  3  5  6  7  9  10  11  13  14  17  18  19  22  23  25  26  27  29
  Count: 20

=== Numbers of form x^2+1 ≤ 200 ===
  2  5  10  17  26  37  50  65  82  101  122  145  170  197
  Count: 14

=== Finding edges (a,b) with a,b allowed, a*b = x^2+1 ===
  (1, 2) -> 2
  (1, 5) -> 5
  (1, 10) -> 10
  (1, 17) -> 17
  (1, 26) -> 26
  (2, 5) -> 10
  (2, 13) -> 26
  (2, 25) -> 50
  (5, 10) -> 50
  (5, 13) -> 65
  (5, 29) -> 145
  (10, 17) -> 170
  (10, 29) -> 290
  (13, 25) -> 325
  (17, 26) -> 442
  Total edges ≤ 30: 15

=== Given values ===
  F(20) = 258
  F(100) = 538768
  F(10^6) = 9851175623

=== Algorithm notes ===
  1. Generate allowed numbers up to N.
  2. Build graph: edge (a,b) if a*b = x^2+1.
  3. Find all simple cycles (length ≥ 3).
  4. Remove rotation/reflection duplicates.
  5. Sum potencies of all distinct bracelets.
  Complexity: exponential in graph size, optimized with DFS.
